e polling average of about 4 points for Acton, recent high-quality surveys, and market pricing near 67-70 percent for Democrats point to a modest Democratic edge, while Ohio's Republican fundamentals and the tossup consensus among most raters temper that lead. The result is a narrow Democratic lean in an open-seat race that remains genuinely competitive.", "watch": "Ramaswamy's heavy spending in the final weeks and any tightening among rural and working-class voters could close the polling gap quickly.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Mike DeWine (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Ohio's open governor's race pits Democrat Amy Acton against Republican Vivek Ramaswamy, with term limits keeping Mike DeWine off the ballot. Polling through early October shows Acton ahead in most surveys, including a New York Times/Siena poll at 49-45 and a Marist poll at 50-44, though a Republican-leaning pollster found a one-point Ramaswamy edge. Averaged across aggregators, Acton's lead sits around three to five points.\n\nMost expert raters call the race a tossup, with one rating it a Democratic lean, and prediction markets give Acton roughly a two-in-three chance. Ramaswamy has far out-raised Acton and holds a large cash advantage, but headlines describe him as struggling in a state no Democrat has carried for governor since 2006. Ohio's Republican-leaning fundamentals keep this competitive, but the weight of recent evidence favors Acton modestly.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.545, "margin": 0.49}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.5929, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.5919, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6166, "margin": 1.3}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.5684, "margin": 1.2}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.592, "margin": 1.4}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6233, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.6597, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.662, "margin": 2.0}, {"date"